 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "No. FAA guidance allows reestablishing control or following loss-of-control procedures rather than mandating immediate landing after lost link; the Matrice 30T manuals describe RTH/land/hover as failsafe actions, and incident reports show RTH was used after loss of signal, not an automatic landing rule.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "FAA guidance does not state an automatic immediate landing after a lost link; it requires considering loss of control and following predefined procedures.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0228",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0049"
      ],
      "quote": "If connection cannot be reestablished, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "conditions": [
       "Loss of control link"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C001",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     },
     {
      "text": "FAA guidance requires the remote PIC to follow pre-determined procedures for loss of VLOS and may include landing or other actions, depending on the situation.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0049"
      ],
      "quote": "The remote PIC or person manipulating the controls should follow pre-determined procedures for the loss of VLOS. ... the remote PIC may need to land the small unmanned aircraft immediately, enter hover mode, or employ a return-to-home sequence.",
      "conditions": [],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C002",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 30T manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "DJI Matrice 30T manuals state that on loss of remote controller signal, action can be set to RTH, land, or hover; RTH path is shown and may continue even if signal is restored.",
      "citations": [
       "dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0033",
       "dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0032"
      ],
      "quote": "The action of the aircraft when the remote controller signal is lost can be set to RTH, land, or hover... The aircraft will start RTH using Advanced RTH... The aircraft will remain in RTH even if the remote controller signal is restored.",
      "conditions": [],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C003",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     },
     {
      "text": "Matrice 30T guidance also notes automated or manual landing during low power or failed RTH, and that auto landing cannot be canceled.",
      "citations": [
       "dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0032"
      ],
      "quote": "If there is sufficient power, the throttle stick can be used to make the aircraft ascend... The aircraft will land automatically if the current battery level can only support the aircraft long enough to descend from its current altitude. Auto landing cannot be canceled.",
      "conditions": [
       "battery constraint"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C004",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "incident:DJI Matrice 30T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 30T incident reports",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "Incident report shows the M30T returning home after a lost link with RTH functioning; another incident cites loss of control with attempted RTH not responding and later regain.",
      "citations": [
       "asrs_dji_m30t_selected_c0002",
